.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt LN 1
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm ln
.Nd make links
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl s Oo Fl F Oc | Fl L | Fl P
.Op Fl f | i
.Op Fl hnvw
.Ar source_file
.Op Ar target_file
.Nm
.Op Fl s Oo Fl F Oc | Fl L | Fl P
.Op Fl f | i
.Op Fl hnvw
.Ar source_file ...
.Ar target_dir
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
makes a new name for a file: a hard link, another directory entry for the
same file, or with
.Fl s
a symbolic link, a small file holding
.Ar source_file
as text, which is followed when the link is used and need not exist.
.Pp
In the first form the link is
.Ar target_file ,
or, when that is a directory, a link in it named after
.Ar source_file Ns 's
last component; with no
.Ar target_file ,
such a link in the working directory.
In the second form each
.Ar source_file
gets such a link in
.Ar target_dir .
A target that exists is an error unless
.Fl f
or
.Fl i
says otherwise.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl F
With
.Fl s ,
replace a target that is an empty directory, instead of linking into it;
implies
.Fl f
unless
.Fl i
is given.
.It Fl f
Remove a target that exists first.
Cancels
.Fl i
and an earlier
.Fl w .
.It Fl h
Don't follow a target that is a symbolic link (to a directory): link in its
place, rather than inside it.
With
.Fl f
this replaces the link.
.It Fl i
Ask, on the standard error, before replacing a target that exists; an answer
beginning with
.Ql y
or
.Ql Y
is yes.
Cancels
.Fl f .
.It Fl L
Hard link what a symbolic link
.Ar source_file
points to, the default.
.It Fl n
The same as
.Fl h .
.It Fl P
Hard link a symbolic link
.Ar source_file
itself.
.It Fl s
Make symbolic links.
.It Fl v
Write each link made, as
.Dq Ar target No => Ar source
.Po
.Dq ->
for a symbolic link
.Pc .
.It Fl w
Warn when a symbolic link's source doesn't exist (relative to the link's
directory).
.El
.Pp
Hard links can't name directories, nor cross file systems.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Point a link at a new version, replacing the old link:
.Dl ln -sfh libfoo.so.2 libfoo.so
.Pp
Link three files into
.Pa bin :
.Dl ln a b c bin
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr link 1 ,
.Xr rm 1 ,
.Xr link 2 ,
.Xr readlink 2 ,
.Xr symlink 2 ,
.Xr symlink 7
.Sh STANDARDS
.Nm
conforms to
.St -p1003.1-2008 ;
.Fl F ,
.Fl h ,
.Fl i ,
.Fl n ,
.Fl v ,
.Fl w
and the one-operand form are extensions, as on the BSDs.
.Sh HISTORY
An
.Nm
command appeared in
.At v1 .
